Changed-By: Lukas Lukic-Spitznagel <lukas.spitznagel@netzint.de>
Description:
 linuxmuster-tools7 - Tools for the linuxmuster.net 7 server.
Changes:
 linuxmuster-tools7 (1:7.4.20~edu) lmn74; urgency=medium
 .
   * edulution fork. The package keeps its upstream name, so the epoch 1: is
     what makes it win against the same package from deb.linuxmuster.net.
   * The version carries the suffix ~edu on top of the epoch, so apt policy,
     dpkg -l and the motd show at a glance that this is the edulution build
     and not the upstream package. "~" sorts before the empty string, so
     1:7.4.20~edu stays below a hypothetical 1:7.4.20 while still outranking
     every upstream 7.x, which carries no epoch at all. The versioned
     dependencies on the fork's own packages therefore clamp on "(>=
     1:x.y.z~)", the Debian idiom that also accepts a tilde suffix.
   * Depend on sophomorix-samba (>= 1:7.4.7~), so the fork cannot be mixed
     with the upstream package.
   * The LDAP settings move from /etc/linuxmuster/webui/config.yml to
     /etc/linuxmuster/tools/ldap.yml, next to password_constraints.yml. The
     old file was created by linuxmuster-webui7 alone, so tools7, cli7 and
     api7 needed the webui installed to reach LDAP at all. The new file uses
     a flat schema and is written by linuxmuster-base7's setup.
   * postinst migrates an existing webui config once
     (install-scripts/migrate_ldap_config.py).
   * ALLOWED_PATHS of lmnfile drops the two webui paths and gains the new
     one.
   * postinst no longer names linuxmuster-webui7, which this fork does not
     install.
   * docs_src/conf.py splits the apt-cache output on the first colon only.
     The epoch adds a second one, so the documented version read as plain
     "1".
   * The github-release job asks for contents: write. The repository's
     default GITHUB_TOKEN permission is read, so creating the release would
     have failed with a 403 on the first tag. Granting it on the job keeps
     the default untouched for every other workflow.
   * Release workflow publishes to edulution-io/edulution-package-server
     instead of linuxmuster/deb, into the Ubuntu codename resolute.
